('128.4.b.12.B',3,'A procedural text such as a recipe lists:','["rhymes", "characters", "jokes", "steps to follow in order"]'::jsonb,3,'Procedural texts give steps.','original'),
('128.4.b.12.C',2,'A letter to a friend usually starts with:','["a greeting", "a map", "a recipe", "a number"]'::jsonb,0,'Letters begin with a salutation.','original'),
('128.4.b.12.C',2,'The part of a letter that comes last is the:','["title", "closing", "heading", "greeting"]'::jsonb,1,'Letters end with a closing and signature.','original'),
('128.4.b.13.A',2,'A good research question is one you can:','["answer with yes or no only", "never answer", "answer using sources", "answer without reading"]'::jsonb,2,'Researchable questions can be answered.','original'),
('128.4.b.13.B',3,'A research plan with adult help lists:','["a snack list", "only the title", "only the answer", "the questions and where to look"]'::jsonb,3,'Plans guide research.','original'),
('128.4.b.13.B',3,'Following a research plan helps you to:','["stay organized", "skip sources", "forget your question", "lose your notes"]'::jsonb,0,'A plan keeps research on track.','original'),
('128.4.b.13.C',3,'A relevant source for a report on elephants is:','["a car manual", "an encyclopedia entry about elephants", "a cookbook", "a sports schedule"]'::jsonb,1,'Relevant sources match the topic.','original'),
('128.4.b.13.C',3,'Gathering relevant information means:','["skipping facts", "copying whole books", "collecting facts that answer your question", "collecting any facts"]'::jsonb,2,'Relevance is key.','original'),
