('128.4.b.6.C',3,'A reader predicts what will happen using:','["the price", "the reader''s age", "text features and clues", "the weight of the book"]'::jsonb,2,'Predictions use evidence.','original'),
('128.4.b.6.C',3,'If a prediction does not match the text, a good reader should:','["stop reading", "ignore the text", "throw the book", "correct the prediction"]'::jsonb,3,'Revise predictions with new information.','original'),
('128.4.b.6.D',2,'Creating mental images helps you to:','["understand the text", "rush", "forget the words", "skip the end"]'::jsonb,0,'Visualizing supports comprehension.','original'),
('128.4.b.6.D',2,'The text says a fox crept through tall dry grass. A reader might picture:','["a snowy town", "a fox in a dry field", "a boat at sea", "a busy street"]'::jsonb,1,'Descriptive words support imagery.','original'),
('128.4.b.6.E',3,'Connecting a text to something happening in society is a:','["new word", "punctuation mark", "text-to-world connection", "spelling pattern"]'::jsonb,2,'Connections link texts to the world.','original'),
('128.4.b.6.E',3,'A story about a storm reminds you of the news. This is a:','["caption", "rhyme", "glossary", "connection to society"]'::jsonb,3,'Connections extend beyond the text.','original'),
('128.4.b.6.F',3,'An inference is supported by:','["evidence from the text", "the cover color", "a friend''s age", "a guess without clues"]'::jsonb,0,'Use evidence for inferences.','original'),
('128.4.b.6.F',3,'A girl yawns, rubs her eyes and goes to bed. You can infer she is:','["hungry", "sleepy", "cold", "excited"]'::jsonb,1,'Clues support inferences.','original'),
('128.4.b.6.G',3,'Evaluating details to determine key ideas means:','["ignoring the main idea", "listing every word", "deciding which details matter most", "counting every detail"]'::jsonb,2,'Key ideas are important details.','original'),
('128.4.b.6.G',3,'In a text about bees, which detail is likely a key idea?','["the page is white", "the font is large", "the title is long", "bees make honey in hives"]'::jsonb,3,'Key ideas are central.','original'),
('128.4.b.6.H',3,'After reading two texts on recycling, you write one idea that uses both. This is:','["synthesis", "rhyming", "copying", "tracing"]'::jsonb,0,'Combining texts is synthesis.','original'),
('128.4.b.6.I',3,'When you notice you are confused, you can monitor comprehension by:','["keeping on without thinking", "using background knowledge or re-reading", "closing the book", "guessing the end"]'::jsonb,1,'Strategies repair comprehension.','original'),
('128.4.b.6.I',3,'Checking a dictionary when you meet a hard word is a way to:','["skip the page", "hide the word", "adjust and keep understanding", "stop reading"]'::jsonb,2,'Resources help adjust.','original'),
('128.4.b.7.A',2,'A personal connection to a text is:','["its page count", "its price", "its shelf number", "how it reminds you of your own life"]'::jsonb,3,'Connections are personal.','original'),
('128.4.b.7.A',2,'After reading about a family dinner, you say it is like yours. This is a:','["personal connection", "map", "title", "new rhyme"]'::jsonb,0,'Describing connections is a response.','original'),
('128.4.b.7.B',3,'A brief comment shows understanding when it:','["says nothing", "says what happened and what you think", "repeats the title", "lists page numbers"]'::jsonb,1,'Comments demonstrate understanding.','original'),
('128.4.b.7.B',3,'Which is a brief written comment about a text?','["The end.", "Good.", "I think the girl was brave because she helped her friend.", "Yes."]'::jsonb,2,'A comment explains thinking.','original'),
('128.4.b.7.C',3,'Text evidence for the idea that a boy is kind could be:','["the book has 20 pages", "the title is long", "he has a red shirt", "he shares his toys with his sister"]'::jsonb,3,'Evidence is a detail from the text.','original'),
('128.4.b.7.C',3,'Using text evidence means:','["supporting your response with details from the text", "making up details", "copying the whole text", "ignoring the text"]'::jsonb,0,'Evidence supports responses.','original'),
('128.4.b.7.D',3,'To paraphrase a text means to:','["skip it", "restate it in your own words", "copy it exactly", "reverse it"]'::jsonb,1,'Paraphrase keeps meaning.','original'),
('128.4.b.7.D',3,'A good retelling keeps the story in:','["no order", "backward order", "logical order", "random order"]'::jsonb,2,'Retelling follows order.','original'),
('128.4.b.7.E',2,'One way to interact with a source is to:','["tear it", "ignore it", "hide it", "illustrate or write about it"]'::jsonb,3,'Illustrating is interaction.','original'),
('128.4.b.7.E',2,'After reading a poem, you might:','["draw a picture of it", "leave it closed", "fold it", "cover it"]'::jsonb,0,'Responses can be visual.','original'),
('128.4.b.7.F',3,'The class learns the word valiente. A student says, El caballero es valiente. This is:','["a title", "responding with new vocabulary", "a rhyme", "a map"]'::jsonb,1,'Use new words in responses.','original'),
('128.4.b.7.F',3,'Using a newly learned word shows that you:','["dislike it", "skipped it", "understand and can use it", "forgot it"]'::jsonb,2,'Applying vocabulary shows learning.','original'),
('128.4.b.8.A',3,'A story shows that working together solves problems. A possible theme is:','["speed", "money", "weather", "teamwork"]'::jsonb,3,'Evidence points to theme.','original'),
('128.4.b.8.B',3,'An internal trait of a character is:','["what the character thinks or feels like", "the size of her shoes", "the color of her shirt", "the length of her hair"]'::jsonb,0,'Internal traits are inside.','original'),
('128.4.b.8.B',3,'An external trait of a character is:','["a secret thought", "something you can see, like height", "a feeling", "a hidden fear"]'::jsonb,1,'External traits can be observed.','original'),
('128.4.b.8.C',3,'The conflict in a story is:','["the title", "the setting", "the problem the characters face", "the page"]'::jsonb,2,'Conflict is the problem.','original'),
('128.4.b.8.C',3,'The resolution is:','["the title", "the first sentence", "the author''s name", "how the conflict is solved"]'::jsonb,3,'Resolution solves the problem.','original'),
('128.4.b.8.D',3,'Setting is important because it:','["affects what happens in the story", "names the book", "names the author", "counts the pages"]'::jsonb,0,'Setting shapes events.','original'),
('128.4.b.8.D',3,'A story set in a desert would most likely include:','["tall forests", "heat and sand", "snowstorms", "ocean waves"]'::jsonb,1,'Setting guides story details.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.A',3,'A common feature of a legend is:','["an index", "a table of contents", "a hero from the past", "a glossary"]'::jsonb,2,'Legends honor heroes.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.B',3,'Stanzas in a poem are:','["titles", "single words", "pictures", "groups of lines"]'::jsonb,3,'Stanzas group lines.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.B',3,'A poem shaped like the thing it describes uses:','["a visual pattern", "a glossary", "no words", "no lines"]'::jsonb,0,'Visual patterns are a poetic structure.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.C',3,'Dialogue in a drama is:','["the stage", "what the characters say", "the title", "the setting"]'::jsonb,1,'Dialogue is spoken.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.C',3,'A play''s setting tells:','["its length only", "its price", "where and when the play happens", "who wrote it"]'::jsonb,2,'Setting is time and place.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.D.i',3,'In an informational text, supporting evidence for a central idea is:','["rhymes", "a title", "jokes", "facts that back up the main point"]'::jsonb,3,'Evidence supports.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.D.i',3,'The central idea of a text about the water cycle is:','["how water moves around the Earth", "how to paint", "how to count", "how to bake"]'::jsonb,0,'Central idea is the main point.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.D.ii',3,'A map in a text helps you to:','["spell words", "find locations", "count lines", "know the author"]'::jsonb,1,'Graphics help locate information.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.D.ii',3,'A timeline helps you to:','["find rhymes", "count syllables", "see events in order", "spell words"]'::jsonb,2,'Timelines show sequence.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.D.iii',3,'Cause and effect stated explicitly uses words like:','["un and una", "pero and aunque", "y and o", "porque and por eso"]'::jsonb,3,'Signal words show cause and effect.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.D.iii',3,'Chronological order tells events:','["in the order they happened", "by size", "in alphabetical order", "by color"]'::jsonb,0,'Chronological means by time.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.E.i',3,'An author says, You should wear a helmet when you ride a bike. The author wants the reader to:','["buy a bike", "put on a helmet", "stop riding", "sell a helmet"]'::jsonb,1,'The author persuades.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.E.i',3,'Persuasive writing states what the author wants you to:','["draw or paint", "rhyme or sing", "think or do", "count or add"]'::jsonb,2,'Persuasion has a purpose.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.E.ii',3,'Which statement can be proven true, so it is a fact?','["The flag is beautiful.", "Everyone loves the flag.", "Texas is the best state.", "Texas has a state flag with a star."]'::jsonb,3,'Facts can be proved.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.E.ii',3,'Which statement tells what someone believes, so it is an opinion?','["Pizza is the tastiest food.", "Pizza is round.", "Pizza is baked.", "Pizza has cheese."]'::jsonb,0,'Opinions state beliefs.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.F',2,'A video with captions and music is:','["a poem only", "a multimodal text", "a glossary", "a printed book only"]'::jsonb,1,'Multimodal uses more than one mode.','original'),
('128.4.b.9.F',3,'A digital text may include:','["only a table of contents", "only footnotes", "hyperlinks and images", "only blank pages"]'::jsonb,2,'Digital texts have links and media.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Spanish Language Arts and English as a Second Language' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
